## 6. Route and role architecture

| Route | Customer | Merchant |
|---|---|---|
| `/notifications/settings` | Canonical Family 5 customer page in `Layout` | Compatibility route to existing Family 4 canonical merchant page |
| `/business/settings/notifications` | Existing authorization denial/redirect behavior | Canonical Family 4 page in merchant workspace/settings shell |
| `/profile` | Editable profile Email destination | Existing role restriction remains |

Final compatibility behavior:

- Unauthenticated: `RequireAuth` redirects to `/login?returnTo=…`.
- Customer opening `/notifications/settings`: mount `CustomerNotificationSettingsPage`.
- Merchant opening `/notifications/settings`: use the role-aware compatibility wrapper to navigate/render the Family 4 canonical experience; never mount a customer form.
- Customer opening `/business/settings/notifications`: retain `RequireBusiness` behavior; do not expose merchant settings.
- Compatibility transitions must pass through dirty-state navigation protection; never silently discard mounted dirty forms.
- Avoid redirect loops by making only the customer route role-aware; merchant canonical route remains guarded.

