- Reduced-motion-compatible sheet and save-bar behavior.
- Sticky save never covers the last control.

## 25. Security contract

- No OTP logging.
- No OTP persistence in browser storage.
- No OTP in route state, URL, analytics, or toast.
- Clear OTP after successful verify and final sheet close.
- Preserve existing CSRF token acquisition, credentialed requests, 401/session-expired behavior.
- Do not expose raw backend/auth claims.
- Do not include verification code in error copy.
- Keep preferences account-level; never duplicate per business.
- Frontend must not expose backend token expiry/attempt information, even though backend internally stores it.

